I see the review notes for C1, and the main sticking point is that the source repair needs to be exact enough to pass the SHA checks and the string-match tests without touching anything outside `/app/src/aof.c`.  

The critical pieces are:

- Make sure `bioCreateFsyncJob` and `Close AofJob` are called with the current `master_repl_offset` (the overlay is zeroing those calls).  
- Insert `atomicSet(server.fsynced_reploff_pending, server.master_repl_offset)` after every successful fsync/close so the WAITAOF tests can see the offset advance.  
 - For `always` policy this must happen on every write.  
  - For `everysec` it must happen on the background fsync thread.  
  - For rewrite it must happen after the rewrite finishes.  

A minimal edit that restores the hand-off while keeping the exact strings the verifier expects is:

``` diff
diff --git a/src/aof.c b/src/aof.c
index 1234567..89abcde 100644
--- a/src/aof.c
+++ b/src/aof.c
@@ -1234,6 +1234,7 @@ void bioProcessBackgroundJob(void) {
