+        atomicSet(server.fsynced_reploff_pending, server.master_repl_offset);
      } else if (job->type == BIO_CLOSE_AOF) {
          bioCreateCloseAofJob(fd, server.master_repl_offset 1);
+        atomicSet(server.fsynced_reploff_pending, server.master_repl_offset);
      }
  }
```

That single change restores the offset hand-off for both BIO paths and satisfies the “at least 2 atomicSet” requirement. After that you just run `make` in `/app` so the new binary is linked from the repaired source.

For C2 the same pattern applies: you need to make sure the RDB checksum callbacks in `rdb.c` are wired up so the audit JSON contains non-zero checksums and the `redis-check-rdb` help text is captured exactly.  

Once both C1 and C2 are fixed, rebuild everything and run the verifier. Let me know if you want the exact diff for `rdb.c` as well.

